    {
      "id": "claim_02260b9d041440448fda65b10f4bc46c",
      "statement": "Connection setup is offer-link driven: the offer peer mints its RSA keypair exactly once per generateOfferLink() invocation (before the peer exists) and creates the RTCPeerConnection (with the shared-predicate-resolved ICE server), data channel, and SDP offer, building the link at most once via a per-invocation offerBuilt flag across the onicecandidate-completion and 3-second timeout paths; regeneration first tears down the previous generation (stale ICE timer cleared, old data channel and peer closed, settled peer crypto and dead-generation UI state reset) and bumps the offerGeneration token so a stale timer can never build a link with the old key. The answer peer decodes the user-controllable offer SDP from the URL inside a try/catch (toast 'Invalid SDP in link' instead of a page crash, PR #45), awaits that promise before createAnswer with a signalingState have-remote-offer check so a rejected setRemoteDescription surfaces an offerFailed error state instead of a stuck spinner (PR #49), awaits the validated p-param key import, generates the answer plus its RSA key pair (when encrypted; an empty-key downgrade is honored via the answer code), and returns the answer code; the channel opens on both sides once the offer peer accepts it (answer SDP decode also guarded with try/catch, toast 'Invalid answer code', PR #45). Once open, both pages wire dataChannel onerror/onclose to the file engines' onChannelClose() so a mid-transfer close surfaces an accurate connection-lost error instead of per-chunk failures (PR #74).",
